## ✅ What was built

**Project:** `SlackChannelDescription`
**Location:** `SlackChannelDescription/Main.xaml`

The workflow does exactly what you asked:

| Step | Activity | What it does |
|------|----------|-------------|
| 1 | **Get Asset** | Reads your Slack Bot Token from an Orchestrator Asset called `SlackBotToken` |
| 2 | **HTTP Request** | Calls `https://slack.com/api/conversations.list` with your token as a Bearer header |
| 3 | **Deserialize JSON** | Parses the API response |
| 4 | **Assign** | Finds the `#office-bellevue` channel in the list |
| 5 | **If / Assign** | Extracts `purpose.value` (the channel description) — handles the case where none is set |
| 6 | **Log Message** | Logs the result to the UiPath output panel |
| 7 | **Message Box** | Pops up a dialog on screen showing the description ✅ |

**Validation:** ✅ `validate` — no errors | ✅ `uip rpa build` — success

